ARCHITECTURE DOCUMENT

Vision:
	Layer 1 - Language
	Responsible for understanding English.
		No reasoning.
		Only language parsing.

	Layer 2 - Knowledge
	Responsible for simple facts.

	Layer 3 - Narrative
	Instead of storing only facts, Genesis stores events.
		This layer preserves the story.

	Layer 4 - Authority
	Genesis doesn't just know who spoke.
		It knows how to rank evidence.
		This layer doesn't change the story.
		It changes how Genesis evaluates the story.

	Layer 5 - Reasoning
	Only after all of the above should Genesis begin asking questions like:
		• Is character 2 quoting character X accurately?
		• Does this statement contradict an earlier statement?
		• Is this an interpretation or a quotation?
		• Can these two passages be reconciled?
		• What conclusions follow from the available evidence?

	Every inference, every answer, every conclusion should have a chain of evidence.

Architecture:
	Layer 1 - Language
	Layer 2 - Knowledge
	Layer 3 - Narrarive
	Layer 4 - Authority
	Layer 5 - Reasoning

